# Allowlist, not a denylist: the context is otherwise ~700 MB (.git, .venv,
# caches) and a denylist grows a hole with every new directory.
#
# CAREFUL: pyproject.toml declares readme = "README.md" and license = {file =
# "LICENSE"} — dropping either fails inside `pip install .`, not as a missing COPY.
*

!titiler
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
